==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Balsam (disambiguation)}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|balsem}}, {{l|en|balsum}}, {{l|en|balsome}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} *{{m|enm||balsam}}, {{m|enm|balsme}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|balsam}}, {{m|ang|balsamum||balsam, balm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|balsamum}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|βάλσαμον||balsam}}, of {{etyl|sem|en}} origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|bôlʹsəm}}, {{IPA|/ˈbɔːlsəm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A sweet-smelling [[oil]] or [[resin]] derived from various plants.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A plant or tree yielding such substance.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} A [[soothing]] [[ointment]].
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|figuratively}} Something soothing.
#: ''Classical music is a sweet '''balsam''' for our sorrows
# A [[flower]]ing plant of the genus ''[[Impatiens]]''.
# The balsam family of flowering plants ([[Balsaminaceae]]), which includes ''[[Impatiens]]'' and {{taxlink|Hydrocera|genus|noshow=1}}.
# A [[balsam fir]] ''[[Abies balsamea]]''.
# [[Canada balsam]], a turpentine obtained from the resin of balsam fir.

